P0001 The review found findings: 2 High, 4 Medium, and 3 Low**. The supplied tests pass, but public API regression probes confirmed five behavioral defects. No production source files were changed; the added tests are in [the scratch harness](/work/tmp/probe/src/lib.rs).
P0002 High
P0003 Async compute operations release their lock before committing the result
P0004 [src/future/value_initializer.rs:350](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:350).
P0005 Expected: Concurrent `and_upsert_with` calls execute serially, as documented in `src/future/entry_selector.rs:335`.
P0006 Observed: `set_waiter_value` consumes the guard and releases the per-key lock before the subsequent insert or removal. Another computation can therefore read the previous value before the first computation commits.
P0007 Evidence: An executed, deterministic single-thread test used an async eviction listener to pause writes. Two upserts both read `10` and left `11`; serialized execution should read `10`, then `11`, and leave `12`. A separate four-worker test also lost increments.
P0008 Consequence: Callers using these APIs for counters or read-modify-write operations can silently lose updates.
P0009 Retain the waiter registration and lock through the completed mutation. Apply the same correction to the analogous `try_compute_if_nobody_else` path and add concurrent regression tests.
P0010 Mixing infallible and unit-error loaders can panic
P0011 Locations: [src/sync/value_initializer.rs:348](/work/crate/src/sync/value_initializer.rs:348), [src/future/value_initializer.rs:592](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:592).
P0012 Expected: `get_with` remains infallible when another caller concurrently uses `try_get_with` on the same key.
P0013 Observed: Both `get_with` and `try_get_with::<_, ()>` use `TypeId::of::<()>()` to identify their waiters. If the fallible loader returns `Err(())`, the infallible loader receives that error and reaches `unreachable!()`.
P0014 Evidence: Executed sync and async tests both panicked at `src/sync/cache.rs:1053` and `src/future/cache.rs:1597`. A control using a different error type passed.
P0015 Consequence: An ordinary loader error can panic another caller whose initializer cannot fail.
P0016 Include the operation kind in waiter identity, or use a private marker type for infallible initialization.
P0017 Medium
P0018 Returning `None` does not clear an already-expired deadline
P0019 Locations: [src/sync/base_cache.rs:689](/work/crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:689), [src/future/base_cache.rs:819](/work/crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:819).
P0020 Expected: `Expiry::expire_after_update` returning `None` clears expiration, as documented in `src/policy.rs`.
P0021 Observed: An elapsed deadline becomes `current_duration = None` because `checked_duration_since` fails. When the callback also returns `None`, the equality check skips clearing the stored deadline.
P0022 Evidence: Executed tests inserted an immediately expired value, then replaced it with a value whose expiry callback returned `None`. Both cache variants returned `None` from the next `get`, instead of the replacement. Clearing an unexpired deadline passed its control test.
P0023 Consequence: A successful replacement can remain immediately expired and unavailable.
P0024 Distinguish an elapsed deadline from an absent deadline, and ensure a callback returning `None` clears the stored timestamp.
P0025 Removal returns values that have already been invalidated
P0026 Cancelling get_with leaves a Computing waiter that blocks later initialization. src/future/value_initializer.rs:239. future::Cache::get_with installs a per-key Computing waiter before awaiting the user initializer, but removes it only when that initializer completes. Polling a get_with whose initializer is pending and then dropping the enclosing future leaves that waiter registered. A later get_with for the same absent key waits on the abandoned computation instead of polling its own initializer, so an ordinary cancelled cache fill prevents a subsequent request from completing.
P0027 Locations: [src/sync/cache.rs:1619](/work/crate/src/sync/cache.rs:1619), [src/future/cache.rs:1964](/work/crate/src/future/cache.rs:1964).
P0028 Expected: Retrieval respects logical invalidation. The compute API also documents `Op::Remove` on an absent entry as returning `StillNone`.
P0029 Observed: Removal clones the physical hash-table value without applying the validity checks used by reads.
P0030 Evidence: Executed sync and async tests inserted `42`, called `invalidate_all`, and confirmed `get` returned `None`. Nevertheless, `remove` returned `Some(42)`. In separate compute tests, the closure received `None`, but returning `Op::Remove` produced `Removed(42)` instead of `StillNone`.
P0031 Consequence: Callers can receive invalidated data and contradictory compute results before maintenance removes the underlying entry.
P0032 Check logical validity when determining the returned value, while still performing physical removal and maintenance bookkeeping.
P0033 Generation wrap prevents maintenance from cleaning up hot entries
P0034 [src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97).
P0035 Expected: The wrapping generation counters continue to distinguish pending updates from fully processed entries.
P0036 Observed: `current >= value` rejects the transition from policy generation `65535` to `0`. Consequently, the entry remains marked dirty after its write operations have been processed.
P0037 Evidence: Executed sync and async tests performed 65,535, 65,536, and 65,537 writes to one key, then invalidated everything and ran maintenance three times. Remaining entry counts were respectively `0`, `1`, and `1`.
P0038 Consequence: Frequently updated entries retain invalidated values and consume capacity after maintenance. Source inspection also shows dirty entries being skipped during eviction.
P0039 Compare generations using wrapping sequence-number ordering, without the ordinary numeric-order rejection. Add wrap-boundary tests.
P0040 Strict documentation builds fail
P0041 Locations: [src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201](/work/crate/src/sync/entry_selector.rs:201), [src/sync/entry_selector.rs:743](/work/crate/src/sync/entry_selector.rs:743), [src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:83](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:83), [src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:99](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:99).
P0042 Expected: Documentation builds successfully with warnings denied.
P0043 Observed: Both public entry-selector examples reference an unresolved `try_append_value_async.rs` link. Documenting private items additionally exposes an unresolved `ptr::eq` link and a bare URL.
P0044 Evidence: Both strict rustdoc commands listed below failed on Rust 1.99.1.
P0045 Consequence: Documentation CI using warnings as errors fails; published API examples contain broken links.
P0046 Reference the defined synchronous example link, qualify `std::ptr::eq`, and mark the URL as a hyperlink.
P0047 Low
P0048 Unsafe ownership and lifetime invariants lack local justification
P0049 Representative locations: [src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:60](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:60), [src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:115](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/arc.rs:115), [src/cht/map/bucket.rs:36](/work/crate/src/cht/map/bucket.rs:36).
P0050 The advisory pass reported **77 unsafe blocks and 13 unsafe implementations** without recognized safety comments. Reviewed examples leave pointer validity, initialization, reference-count ownership, or thread-safety reasoning implicit.
P0051 This makes changes to these internal abstractions harder to validate. Add local explanations of the required invariants. This is a maintainability finding, not a demonstrated memory-safety defect.
P0052 invalidate_all exposes older cached values until maintenance runs. src/sync/base_cache.rs:406. In sync::Cache, invalidate_all only records valid_after and leaves the hash-table entries in place. For a previously inserted entry whose last-modified time is strictly earlier than that cutoff, a get or contains_key immediately after invalidate_all still reads the old mapping until a maintenance pass removes it. A caller that invalidates the cache after refreshing its backing data can therefore continue serving the obsolete value even though invalidation has returned.
P0053 Public API behavior is undocumented
P0054 Representative locations: [src/future/entry_selector.rs:242](/work/crate/src/future/entry_selector.rs:242), [src/future/entry_selector.rs:897](/work/crate/src/future/entry_selector.rs:897).
P0055 The advisory pass identified **23 undocumented public items**, including items exposed through re-exports and the unstable debug-counter feature. In particular, neither `and_try_compute_if_nobody_else` method explains when it skips computation or what it returns under contention.
P0056 Callers must inspect implementation details to use these methods correctly. Document their contention behavior, results, and errors. The pass also reported 20 missing formal `# Errors` sections; several already describe errors in prose.
P0057 Eight public types lack `Debug`
P0058 Representative locations: [src/future.rs:58](/work/crate/src/future.rs:58), [src/future/builder.rs:58](/work/crate/src/future/builder.rs:58), [src/common/iter.rs:22](/work/crate/src/common/iter.rs:22).
P0059 The advisory pass confirmed missing `Debug` implementations on two builders, four entry selectors, and two iterator types. Callers cannot format these handles for diagnostics or derive `Debug` on enclosing types that contain them.
P0060 Add implementations that expose useful state without requiring callback closures themselves to implement `Debug`.
P0139 Borrowed-key fallible entry lookup returns an entry whose key panics
P0140 [src/sync/cache.rs:1422](/work/crate/src/sync/cache.rs:1422), [src/common/entry.rs:59](/work/crate/src/common/entry.rs:59).
P0141 On a cache hit, `entry_by_ref(...).or_try_insert_with(...)` should return an `Entry` containing its key. The lookup instead hardcodes `need_key = false`. Calling `key()`, or formatting the entry with `Debug`, then panics with `Bug: Key is None`.
P0142 Executed regressions reproduce this in both `sync::Cache` and `SegmentedCache`. The corresponding asynchronous test passes. The existing doctest checks the key after insertion but omits that assertion on the subsequent hit.
P0143 forward `need_key` and test both insertion and hit paths.
P0144 Clearing expiration can leave a dangling timer handle
P0145 [src/common/timer_wheel.rs:493](/work/crate/src/common/timer_wheel.rs:493).
P0146 When a scheduled entry’s expiration becomes `None`, advancing the timer wheel should remove the timer and clear its stored handle. The `None` branch instead drops the popped node without clearing the handle in `DeqNodes`.
P0147 An executed unit regression schedules an entry, clears expiration through a read performed by `or_insert_with_if`, advances the mocked clock, and runs maintenance. It confirms that expiration is cleared while `timer_node()` remains set.
P0148 Source inspection shows subsequent removal or rescheduling can pass this freed node to pointer-dereferencing timer operations. The regression stops at checking the stale handle; it does not exercise that subsequent dereference.
P0149 clear the handle before dropping the node and handle this path as a descheduling event.
P0150 Medium
P0151 Asynchronous entry computations can lose updates
P0152 [src/future/value_initializer.rs:350](/work/crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:350), also line 488.
P0153 The documented entry-computation contract serializes calls on the same key. Instead, `set_waiter_value` removes the waiter and releases its lock before the resulting cache operation completes.
P0154 An executed deterministic regression starts a counter at zero and performs three concurrent `and_upsert_with` increments. An asynchronous eviction listener waits during the first replacement. The other two computations both read `1`, leaving the final value at `2` instead of `3`.
P0155 retain the computation guard through completion of the cache operation, preserving cancellation cleanup.
P0156 Returning `None` from expiry update can leave the replacement expired
P0157 [src/sync/base_cache.rs:689](/work/crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:689), [src/future/base_cache.rs:819](/work/crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:819).
P0158 `Expiry::expire_after_update` documents that returning `None` clears expiration. For an already-expired deadline, `checked_duration_since` produces `None`. When the callback also returns `None`, the equality check skips clearing the stored deadline.
P0159 Executed sync and future regressions configure a 20 ms creation expiry, wait 40 ms, and replace the value with an update callback explicitly returning `None`. An immediate `get` returns `None` instead of the newly inserted value.
P0160 distinguish an elapsed deadline from absent expiration and ensure an explicit `None` clears the stored deadline.
P0161 Removal returns values already invalidated by `invalidate_all`
P0162 contains_key refreshes time-to-idle on successful membership checks. src/sync/base_cache.rs:204. The sync::Cache contains_key lookup treats a successful hash-table lookup as an access and advances the entry's last-accessed timestamp. With a ten-second time-to-idle, inserting at t=0 and calling contains_key at t=9 keeps the entry readable after t=10. Repeated membership checks therefore extend cache lifetime even though the public contract says that contains_key does not reset idle timers.
P0163 [src/sync/cache.rs:1620](/work/crate/src/sync/cache.rs:1620), [src/future/cache.rs:1964](/work/crate/src/future/cache.rs:1964).
P0164 The invalidation contract guarantees that retrieval methods do not return invalidated entries. Removal clones the raw table value without applying the validity checks used by `get`.
P0165 Executed tests in both implementations show:
P0166 - After inserting `1` and calling `invalidate_all`, `remove` returns `Some(1)`.
- An `and_compute_with` closure receives `None`, returns `Op::Remove`, and receives `CompResult::Removed` containing that invalidated value. The documented result for an absent entry is `StillNone`.
P0167 apply visibility checks to returned values while still removing the underlying entry and completing maintenance.
P0168 Out-of-order write logs permanently distort weighted size
P0169 [src/sync/base_cache.rs:1460](/work/crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:1460), [src/future/base_cache.rs:1611](/work/crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:1611).
P0170 After completed writes and maintenance, weighted size should converge to the stored entries’ weight. Applying each update’s old/new delta with saturating subtraction loses information when logs arrive out of order.
P0171 Executed sync and future regressions pause one update inside an expiry callback, allowing a later update to be processed first. The sole stored value weighs `3`, but maintenance reports `4`. Removing that entry leaves an empty cache reporting weight `1`.
P0172 This creates persistent accounting errors that affect capacity decisions.
P0173 track the weight actually applied to policy state per entry and reconcile updates by generation.
P0174 Generation wrap prevents maintenance from removing entries
P0175 [src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97](/work/crate/src/common/concurrent/entry_info.rs:97).
P0176 `entry_gen` wraps as a `u16`, but `set_policy_gen` rejects numerically smaller generations even when they are newer after wrapping. The entry consequently remains marked dirty, and maintenance skips it.
P0177 Executed sync and future tests perform maintenance after every replacement, then call `invalidate_all` and repeatedly run maintenance. After 65,534, 65,535 and 65,536 replacements, remaining entry counts are `[0, 1, 1]`; all should be zero. Reads correctly hide the retained entry.
P0178 Ordinary frequently updated keys can therefore retain invalidated values and consume capacity indefinitely without another explicit removal.
P0179 use consistent modular generation ordering and add wrap-boundary tests.
